      "problem": "What is the volume of a sphere whose diameter is $18 \\:\\textrm{cm}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We can find the volume of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nV = \\dfrac 4 3 \\pi r^3 ,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $r=\\dfrac{18}{2}=9\\:\\textrm{cm}$ into the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV = \\dfrac 4 3 \\pi \\left(9\\right)^3 \n \t\t= 972\\pi \\:\\textrm{cm}^3.\n$$",
